d cover-ups, that was one good scenario. I had the feeling it could go for a full-fledged space game, weird, dark and retro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>\u03a8</b></i> The Corps is Father. The Corps is Mother. <i><b>\u03a8</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26309-al-bester","name":"Al Bester","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T17:18:44-08:00","id":1429796,"title":"","content":"Also don't forget that both Quantum and Noetic societies, absent interference, appear to, if they survive, transcend and level the universe. so it's not so much dead as &quot;a lot of them took off for other realms.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not certain, since Talented societies are called out as not transcending in the same way, why we don't see them, but they may have some other form of transformation. <br /> <br /> So in Trinity, even societies separated by only a few hundred thousand years may never see each other, because the earlier one has <i>left.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T16:29:11-08:00","id":1429910,"title":"","content":"There is a piece in the Aeon book about this. Pages 362-363 if that helps at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T06:11:08-08:00","id":1429934,"title":"","content":"Ohhhh<br /> <br /> Alfred Bester. The Green Lantern guy. I get it lol.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I love this idea. Good luck turning it into a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T06:18:42-08:00","id":1429935,"title":"","content":"How is this research?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T18:15:53-08:00","id":1430016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1429703-article-the-milky-way-is-probably-full-of-dead-civilizations-spoilers?p=1429935#post1429935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this research?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mathematical modeling of our anxieties, I guess.<br /> <br /> I mean, we barely stood up and went to the Moon just to sit, fat and flat, back on the couch and suddenly we can mathematically predict the ins and outs of the universe's life forms? Not to mention, the intelligent ones, having so far just ONE planet to base all this?<br /> <br /> Come on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>\u03a8</b></i> The Corps is Father. The Corps is Mother. <i><b>\u03a8</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26309-al-bester","name":"Al Bester","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T10:18:07-08:00","id":1430343,"title":"","content":"If you haven't already read it, Distant Worlds has a lot of neat stuff like this. Mysteriously vanishing civilzations with new hostile civilizations growing in their shadows, civilizations wiped out for unknown reasons, civilizations wiped out from known reasons and how trying to evade those reasons while studying them. Neat hooks, and some cool new tech to go along with it. Not to mention rules for playing a Qin, which I recently used and heartily enjoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmo